{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "034D", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-descending-properties-smooth}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bedf382079bd0734009767381f91666f4304179be6b7e663eb550f86b6b52658", "source_text": "Properties of schemes local in the smooth topology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:899eda64743bd3afbd0bd2eb0b910dfb1b3a99374c8f6662edd7d4f564d19176", "unit_id": "tag:034D:title"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "034D", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b3b81f76b763f5f4f8d15688125f518dce902de317c7ac1a31bfca0a462805d0", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we find some properties of schemes which are local on the base\nin the smooth topology.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:64e805fc984b85432d3110d54a8cb12866702ed2b9691a0253c445f06648e1df", "unit_id": "tag:034D:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "034D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(S) =$", "MATH_0002": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-reduced-local-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d9e523b5d771727c8fe8b5d75c14dcd897bde16ff6e9510a3b1f2494e83f4494", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:566d3b5c63dcd7ae853efcbf525c90b972335e053e3c5dd5157de79b0467eed6", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is reduced'' is local in the smooth\ntopology.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:acddfeb9e6f3635384dab5424bb66bbfe8c804ac77d23454dae6b77d7c33e989", "unit_id": "tag:034E:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "034D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$S'$", "MATH_0004": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$S'$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-definition-reduced}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-reduced-goes-up}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-descent-reduced}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4165f0d6b3d7c9e9ca3ca1d702af6fea3614a4ed908037664dc9af089c2b641c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f4179ca3611ebee035e1e419c707f8727b0a5488c991b784fc1f4bf1abd09ff7", "source_text": "We will use Lemma <REF_0001>.\nFirst we note that ``being reduced'' is local\nin the Zariski topology. This is clear from the definition,\nsee Schemes, Definition <REF_0002>.\nNext, we show that if <MATH_0001> is a smooth morphism of affines\nand <MATH_0002> is reduced, then <MATH_0003> is reduced. This is\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nFinally, we show that if <MATH_0004> is a surjective\nsmooth morphism of affines\nand <MATH_0005> is reduced, then <MATH_0006> is reduced. This is\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0004>.\nThus (1), (2) and (3) of Lemma <REF_0005> hold\nand we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d3d618eec10f9697c2bd7f2fe09e2a865e7a193da5fe737623fccd69b1ae73be", "unit_id": "tag:034E:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "034D", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nNormality is local in the smooth topology.\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(S) =$", "MATH_0002": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-normal-local-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d9e523b5d771727c8fe8b5d75c14dcd897bde16ff6e9510a3b1f2494e83f4494", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5671df5ada9760ef3d0bc875d46b6914ee49bc99ecc9b088d683a554f2c67ac3", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nThe property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is normal'' is local in the smooth\ntopology.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:83397248af09e5f2c72faa9f62cf09a2c1fc46db53af162ea5ae5b559f469c6d", "unit_id": "tag:034F:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "034D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$S'$", "MATH_0004": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$S'$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{properties-definition-normal}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-normal-goes-up}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-descent-normal}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4165f0d6b3d7c9e9ca3ca1d702af6fea3614a4ed908037664dc9af089c2b641c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:607b162d3f4c5f3da30cd24592b4103a0e9261c14e3be3c52886d6acf978da91", "source_text": "We will use Lemma <REF_0001>.\nFirst we show ``being normal'' is local\nin the Zariski topology. This is clear from the definition,\nsee Properties, Definition <REF_0002>.\nNext, we show that if <MATH_0001> is a smooth morphism of affines\nand <MATH_0002> is normal, then <MATH_0003> is normal. This is\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nFinally, we show that if <MATH_0004> is a surjective\nsmooth morphism of affines\nand <MATH_0005> is normal, then <MATH_0006> is normal. This is\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0004>.\nThus (1), (2) and (3) of Lemma <REF_0005> hold\nand we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a6954a66375f7f145ca5b92f5b88b432ca71bcba4576aee765e4d60d5c686e38", "unit_id": "tag:034F:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "034D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(S) =$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$(R_k)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-Rk-local-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4a84fc2f202e05d989d4be997d37563bf8191d3a7d81bb107a2c3e6e79685250", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:94a2ca61831746858221afe5177deb77b28189963491b6130f57ba8ae413252d", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is locally Noetherian and <MATH_0003>''\nis local in the smooth topology.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:96fef04b9253c0876ad2096c9755769b0a6fca576382f81d9639bae969e26d1a", "unit_id": "tag:036C:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "034D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0002": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0005": "$S'$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0007": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0008": "$S'$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0010": "$S$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-smooth-flat}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-smooth-locally-finite-presentation}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-Noetherian-local-fppf}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{properties-definition-Rk}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-Rk-goes-up}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-smooth-characterize}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-base-change-smooth}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-characterize-smooth-over-field}", "REF_0010": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-descent-Rk}", "REF_0011": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1161b0262695760e5a074768286ba2c28d47931dd9daccc7a82448ab30a2e60d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d985acb2ca582bb1802f5601054a57b21ff2f1ddcfb6ba50a94279f4f1085a52", "source_text": "We will check (1), (2) and (3) of Lemma <REF_0001>.\nAs a smooth morphism is flat of finite presentation\n(Morphisms, Lemmas <REF_0002>\nand <REF_0003>)\nwe have already checked this for ``being locally Noetherian'' in the proof\nof Lemma <REF_0004>.\nWe will use this without further mention in the proof.\nFirst we note that <MATH_0001> is local in the Zariski topology.\nThis is clear from the definition,\nsee Properties, Definition <REF_0005>.\nNext, we show that if <MATH_0002> is a smooth morphism of affines\nand <MATH_0003> has <MATH_0004>, then <MATH_0005> has <MATH_0006>. This\nis Algebra, Lemmas <REF_0006>\n(use Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0007>,\nAlgebra, Lemmas <REF_0008>\nand <REF_0009>).\nFinally, we show that if <MATH_0007> is a surjective\nsmooth morphism of affines and <MATH_0008> has <MATH_0009>,\nthen <MATH_0010> has <MATH_0011>. This is\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0010>.\nThus (1), (2) and (3) of Lemma <REF_0011> hold\nand we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7f546356c269cd082b6153650f1dcde323c08e39efd52a59cbc0039cceb6e397", "unit_id": "tag:036C:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "034D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(S) =$", "MATH_0002": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-regular-local-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d9e523b5d771727c8fe8b5d75c14dcd897bde16ff6e9510a3b1f2494e83f4494", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9c7034e3e53e41f869338459bc0dd8296cb0efc05953da7fcabfa103982c2a89", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is regular''\nis local in the smooth topology.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2a68a0d8654796bc4b70e9d06592492391179b11f167fee275e519f235617699", "unit_id": "tag:036D:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "034D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(R_k)$", "MATH_0002": "$k \\geq 0$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-Rk-local-smooth}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e99a5117b5c9ff8e72af7cec46907d831b71c9c484016161c6f4ba2ae11cf6f1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c2ae7e8ae33d8d07b5240b892da655d4cf97e2ff1835018faf98a37940f57b31", "source_text": "This is clear from Lemma <REF_0001>\nabove since a locally Noetherian scheme is regular if and only if\nit is locally Noetherian and <MATH_0001> for all <MATH_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cd8a5941071a88162d391f5e565dd5b640a6ae6ee141399e7d37752b4a6d5d0b", "unit_id": "tag:036D:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "034D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}(S) =$", "MATH_0002": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-Nagata-local-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d9e523b5d771727c8fe8b5d75c14dcd897bde16ff6e9510a3b1f2494e83f4494", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:77e61dd94dcb7f30dd29a1c349d37d85f6553a6e2ad57d7b5a0c51970f26d0e7", "source_text": "The property <MATH_0001>``<MATH_0002> is Nagata''\nis local in the smooth topology.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:819d067800ec9d84348125b36b58f7a3ad7715e9ed08fbdcf466b0e54fa6b495", "unit_id": "tag:036E:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "034D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$S'$", "MATH_0004": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$S'$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{properties-lemma-locally-nagata}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-finite-type-nagata}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-descent-nagata}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-descending-properties}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4165f0d6b3d7c9e9ca3ca1d702af6fea3614a4ed908037664dc9af089c2b641c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cecd735bdae0fc1cc30a4e99b4c1521db3c3f42dd01c0f7be9697ecb1d1b7fbf", "source_text": "We will check (1), (2) and (3) of Lemma <REF_0001>.\nFirst we note that being Nagata is local in the Zariski topology.\nThis is Properties, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nNext, we show that if <MATH_0001> is a smooth morphism of affines\nand <MATH_0002> is Nagata, then <MATH_0003> is Nagata. This\nis Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nFinally, we show that if <MATH_0004> is a surjective\nsmooth morphism of affines and <MATH_0005> is Nagata,\nthen <MATH_0006> is Nagata. This is\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0004>.\nThus (1), (2) and (3) of Lemma <REF_0005> hold\nand we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6d121436f28fddd3d1492c236fea56ad5ad8f80b1e486a640fca0b39d0b4c4da", "unit_id": "tag:036E:proof"}
